From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wintrust: create catalogs from catalog definition files

CryptCATCDFOpen/Close/EnumCatAttributes/EnumMembersByCDFTagEx,
CryptCATOpen(CREATENEW), CryptCATPutCatAttrInfo/PutMemberInfo/PutAttrInfo,
CryptCATPersistStore and CryptSIPCreateIndirectData (flat files and PE
images) were stubs. A catalog is built as a CTL in an unsigned PKCS#7
message: the catalog written from the definition file of Wine's own test
is byte for byte the catalog Windows' makecat made from it (apart from the
list identifier and the time). 41 todo_wine marks are removed from
dlls/wintrust/tests/crypt.c.

Gate: test/wintrustcatw-gate.sh (64 and 32 bit). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_CAT_NODEDUP, _FILEORDER, _EMPTYATTRS, SG_MUTANT_CDF_SHARING, _NOCB, SG_MUTANT_PE_HASH and
SG_MUTANT_SIP_COUNT are caught.
